    schema:datePosted "2026-09-08"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Get to know us Ideals is a global B2B SaaS product company recognized as the most highly rated and customer-centric brand in the secure business collaboration market. Trusted by over 2,000,000 users from 300,000 companies globally, we help people run high-stakes processes and make important decisions with less stress, higher quality, and shorter hours. Ideals Virtual Data Room (VDR): Secure document sharing and collaboration for due diligence, fundraising, corporate reporting, licensing, clinical trials, and other complex transactions. Ideals Board: Board and leadership collaboration platform for faster, safer, and more compliant decision-making. The role Ideals is uniquely positioned to redefine the VDR industry. Now we aim to own the upmarket M&A segment and establish Ideals as the Tier 1 brand in that space - translating market leadership into stronger brand equity, pipeline, and revenue. We're looking for a VP of Marketing to make this happen. You'll lead a high-performing global team and shape the marketing function end-to-end: positioning and category authority, a scalable demand engine, and the operating system behind it. This is a builder's role for a strategic, data-driven leader who wants their work to show up in commercial results, not just in brand tracking. This is a fully remote role for candidates based in the UK, Ireland, Switzerland, or the Netherlands. What you will do Define how Ideals wins You'll own positioning, messaging, competitive intelligence, and GTM plans across every product, segment, and region – the strategic foundation everything else in marketing builds on. Build category authority From industry events, reports, and benchmarks to media relations, executive visibility, and speaking programmes - you'll make Ideals the name the upmarket M&A segment thinks of first, and keep every external touchpoint aligned with our brand positioning. Turn attention into pipeline You'll drive demand generation across paid and organic channels, ABM, content, and nurture, then guide the team capturing it through search, review platforms, intent data, and conversion optimisation. As the Key Accounts Sales team scales, you'll direct regional programmes into each market's sales plan and own the result end to end against pipeline and revenue targets. Run marketing as a system You'll own the martech and analytics stack, attribution, KPI framework, and ROI reporting – plus the marketing budget, agencies, and strategic vendors – so every decision is data-driven, and every dollar is accountable. Lead the people who make it happen You'll hire, develop, and lead a global team, and work shoulder to shoulder with Sales, Product, and Customer Success to drive cohesive business growth. What you bring 10+ years of B2B marketing experience, with a strong SaaS background 4+ years in a senior marketing leadership role within a fast-growing company, with responsibility for the broader marketing function Proven experience leading and scaling diverse high-performing marketing teams, including hiring, talent development, and performance management Brand marketing portfolio with proven activation expertise across diverse channels and markets Hands-on experience across content, design, and growth initiatives, with the ability to go deep when needed Track record scaling digital and field marketing programs that measurably grew pipeline and revenue Solid understanding of demand generation and ABM initiatives Successful track record of implementing marketing initiatives based on analytical and data-driven decisions Excellent communication and problem-solving skills with a can-do attitude Fluency in English (C1+ level) Nice to have Experience in M&A, Investment Banking, or Financial Services, with a strong understanding of the dealmaking ecosystem What we offer We highly value our people, so we will empower you with all the resources and support to help you reach your full potential. For your best work Remote-first flexibility to shape your ideal workday Home workplace budget Co-working expense coverage Individual IT budget for extra equipment Top-tier tech and AI-powered tools For your growth Access to Ideals Academy with numerous courses Investment in external learning and development activities Guidance in Personal Development Plan creation Professional literature and subscriptions coverage Support of your passion as a speaker or writer Internal talent mobility opportunities For your well-being Tailored Wellness Package for your physical and mental health Funding for sports competitions Paid health-related time-off 25 business days of annual leave Nest Pensions scheme contribution Extra perks Budget for meetups with your local team Generous internal referral program Our culture Commitment, Excellence, Collaboration, Trust and Care are core values to the Ideals team. For us, these are the principles that every Idealer lives and breathes. We are on the lookout for like-minded individuals who share our values. By doing so, we create a team where talents feel at ease and work to the best of their abilities. Discover more. Ideals is an equal opportunity employer Ideals is made up of people from a wide variety of backgrounds and lifestyles. We embrace diversity and invite applications from people from all walks of life. We don’t discriminate against employees or applicants based on gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, race, religion, age, national origin, or citizenship. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
