    schema:description "Your area of responsibility Join us as a Working Student (m/f/d) and become part of our new Calibration Team in the Dresden area (Dippoldiswalde)! From the very beginning, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute your ideas and help shape and develop our new business area. You can look forward to a variety of exciting responsibilities, including: Performing in-house calibrations of measuring equipment Carrying out adjustments and minor repairs on measuring equipment Performing DGUV V3 electrical safety inspections Evaluating and documenting measurement results Supporting the maintenance and expansion of our accreditation Continuously improving our measurement and calibration processes Your profile Currently pursuing a degree in Electrical Engineering or a comparable field of study Good working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications Strong commitment to quality and a detail-oriented approach to work Strong teamwork and communication skills, combined with the ability to work independently Very good command of German; good command of English is a plus We offer A varied, challenging, and never boring role Flexible hours that work with your study schedule A supportive team that values you and helps you grow The opportunity to be part of a new project from the very beginning and contribute your own ideas If you meet the qualifications and are interested in this exciting opportunity, we look forward to receiving your application - including your cover letter, CV, proof of enrollment, certificates and / or references. The protection of your personal data is very important to us. Further information on data processing in the application process can be found in our privacy policy at the following link: https://iocto.com/en/data-protection/ We look forward to getting to know you! Contact iocto GmbH Lorsbacher Straße 31 65719 Hofheim am Taunus Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
