    schema:datePosted "2026-09-08"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Q ENERGY is Europe’s 360° green energy company. Together with our more than 500 employees we develop, build, and manage renewable energy assets across the entire value chain of large-scale renewable energy projects – from solar, to onshore wind and offshore wind, to energy storage and hybrid power plants. With a pipeline of more than 11 GW we are among the leading renewable energy companies in Europe. We are always on the lookout for people who want to work with us to empower a sustainable world with green energy. As a Working Student in Central Europe Finance, you will support our finance team in the daily operations of our Central European entities. This role offers hands-on exposure to operational accounting, closing procedures, audit support, and cross-border financial coordination in an international environment. Your Responsibilities Support day-to-day accounts payable and accounts receivable processes. Assist with monthly, quarterly, and year-end closing activities for our Central European entities. Maintain financial records with a high level of accuracy, completeness, and integrity. Prepare and organize documentation for internal and external audits. Coordinate with various departments to resolve billing discrepancies and ensure smooth cross-border financial workflows. Support compliance with internal accounting standards and relevant statutory requirements. Apply and further develop your understanding of HGB in practical accounting processes. Requirements You are currently studying Business, Finance, Accounting, or a related field. You have a strong foundation in double-entry bookkeeping and general financial principles. You bring solid HGB knowledge. You are fluent in German and English, both written and spoken, with business-fluent communication skills in both languages. You are comfortable working with German tax and accounting documents and participating in English-speaking regional meetings. You have a reliable, diligent, and highly detail-oriented working style. You take ownership of your tasks and treat accuracy as a non-negotiable standard. Willingness to work on-site in the office, as we believe face-to-face collaboration is essential for learning the nuances of Central European accounting Benefits We offer an hourly salary of 15€ for Bachelor and 17€ for Master students. Additionally, we off the following benefits: Our workplace: Located in a modern and sustainable office building just a few steps from Südkreuz station, making it easily accessible for all employees. IT Equipment: We’ll set you up with a laptop, monitor, headphones, and, if needed, a company phone. Work-Life Balance: we value your personal time. Enjoy the flexibility to choose your work hours, so you can prioritize what matters most—whether it’s attending a workout class, handling personal matters, or starting your weekend a little earlier. You’re in control. Mobile Working: At Q ENERGY we offer a hybrid work model: three days in the office and two days of mobile working. This setup supports in-person teamwork while also allowing for more flexibility and reduced commuting. Spendit Card: €25 monthly allowance on top of your monthly salary, which can be used for your daily lunch or can be saved up unlimitedly. Public Transport Allowance: Enjoy a €15 monthly contribution to your BVG ticket—making your commute easier and more affordable! Generous Vacation Policy: Enjoy a well-deserved break and take 31 vacation days a year to relax, recharge, and explore! Onboarding: We provide a detailed onboarding process to ensure you have a smooth and successful start with us, helping you feel supported and prepared from day one. Pension Plan: We contribute €13.29 each month to your pension. Corporate Discounts: Employees get access to exclusive offers and discounts for various brands through our Corporate Benefits program. Corporate Health Management: Prioritize your well-being with our corporate health management program, including preventive check-ups to keep you at your best! Mutual support: You’ll thrive in a supportive environment where open communication, teamwork, and knowledge sharing are highly valued. We’re committed to your growth, encouraging your professional and personal development through ongoing support and guidance. Would you like to become part of Q ENERGY? Then we look forward to receiving your application. Please let us know your salary expectations and your earliest possible starting date. Please note: We do not accept applications by email. Please use the \"Apply now\" button for your application. Thank you very much! If you have any questions, please contact our recruiting team: ----- Q ENERGY is an internationally operating company - at our company, people from many nations, cultures, and locations work together in partnership and exchange their experiences and values with each other in an open and collegial manner. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
